1 2 3 4  0 pick-ref .  3 pick-ref .  0 pick .  3 pick .  2drop 2drop
: same ( lo hi u -- flag ) >r 2dup r@ um/mod-ref 2swap r> um/mod rot = -rot = and ;
100 0 7 same .  -1 0 10 same .  0 1 2 same .  -1 5 6 same .  12345678901234 9876 99999 same .
100 0 7 um/mod-ref . .  0 1 2 um/mod-ref u. .
: agree ( addr u -- flag ) 2dup latest @ search-list >r latest @ search-list-ref r> = ;
s" dup" agree .  s" DUP" agree .  s" no-such-word" agree .  s" agree" agree .
s" Swap" latest @ search-list 0<> .  s" no-such-word" latest @ search-list .
\ SHA256-BLOCK against COMPRESS-REF: two blocks, chained
create blk64 64 allot  : fill64 ( -- ) 64 0 do i 37 * 11 + blk64 i + c! loop ;  fill64
create state1 8 cells allot
sha-init blk64 compress blk64 compress  sha-h state1 8 cells-move
sha-init blk64 compress-ref blk64 compress-ref  sha-h 8 cells state1 8 cells compare 0= .
\ CMOVE, CMOVE> and FILL against their Forth definitions, overlapping both ways
create m1 40 allot  create m2 40 allot
: setup ( -- ) 40 0 do  i 3 * dup m1 i + c!  m2 i + c!  loop ;
: same? ( -- flag ) m1 40 m2 40 compare 0= ;
setup  m1 m1 7 + 20 cmove  m2 m2 7 + 20 cmove-ref  same? .
setup  m1 7 + m1 20 cmove>  m2 7 + m2 20 cmove>-ref  same? .
setup  m1 3 + 30 $5a fill  m2 3 + 30 $5a fill-ref  same? .
setup  m1 m2 0 cmove  m1 0 0 fill  same? .  m1 1+ c@ .
